      "prompt": "Tried recreating this viral video, ideas by two of my favorites @techhalla and @TechieBySA. I only had 10 minutes to do it, so there we go :) \n\nHere is the prompt I use for the image with Nano Banana: \n\ngenerate a realistic live-broadcast-style image of [primary_role] inside [primary_context], but with one visually iconic element inferred from [crossover_domain].\n<instructions: argentina vs spain world cup final, 120th minute, spain leading 1-0, argentina player paredes with a steel chair in hand, time noon, >\nrules:\n- infer primary_context accurately from primary_role\n- preserve the normal uniform, venue, crowd, lighting, camera angle, and seriousness of the scene\n- infer crossover_gear from crossover_domain\n- the crossover element must be physically worn, held, or used by the subject in a believable way\n- the subject should behave as if this strange crossover is normal\n- the humor comes from the clash between serious context and inappropriate-but-realistic gear\n- keep the image grounded, candid, and broadcast-like\n- optional scoreboard, tv overlay, sideline figures, crowd blur, field/court/stage depth if relevant\n- no hard-coded sport, country, team, equipment, player, stadium, score, or overlay unless supplied <instructions>",
      "prompt_ko": "'[primary_role]이 [primary_context] 안에 있는 실사 생중계 이미지 + [crossover_domain]에서 추론한 시각적으로 상징적인 요소 1개'라는 구조. 규칙이 유머의 설계도 — ①역할에서 맥락을 정확히 추론 ②평소의 유니폼·경기장·관중·조명·카메라 앵글·진지함을 그대로 보존 ③크로스오버 장비는 실제로 착용/파지/사용되며 물리적으로 믿을 만하게 ④피사체는 이 기묘함이 정상인 것처럼 행동 ⑤웃음은 '진지한 맥락 vs 부적절하지만 사실적인 장비'의 충돌에서 나옴 ⑥이미지는 담백하고 캔디드하며 중계 화면답게. 스코어보드·TV 오버레이·사이드라인 인물·관중 블러는 선택. 종목·국가·팀·장비·선수·경기장·점수 하드코딩 금지.",
      "gen_prompt": "A realistic live-broadcast-style photograph of a world chess championship final, shot from the standard television camera angle. The grandmaster sits at the board mid-game in a hushed wood-panelled hall under stage lighting, his opponent opposite him and an arbiter standing nearby, the audience blurred in the dark background. He is wearing full ice-hockey goaltender gear: chest protector, blocker, catching glove resting beside the clock, and a painted mask pushed up onto his forehead. He behaves as though this is completely normal, brow furrowed in deep concentration, one gloved hand hovering over a bishop. The venue, lighting, camera angle and seriousness of the broadcast are entirely preserved, with a lower-third scoreboard overlay and a move clock. Candid, grounded, broadcast-like realism; the humor comes purely from the clash between the solemn context and the incongruous but physically believable gear.",
