      "title": "★프롬프트를 방정식으로 — (주제) + (요소들) − (원치 않는 것) = [출력], 더하기·빼기 연산자로 스타일을 합성",
      "prompt": "I asked GPT to show me a bunch street foods from the Middle East. I don't think I have tried any of them. \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 lesser known Middle Eastern hidden gem street food [EQUATION] \n\n($ SUBJECT)\n+ (giant edible landscape)\n+ (tiny worker typography world)\n+ (open-book clay story diorama)\n+ (soft pastel textile relief)\n+ (object-shaped flat-lay infographic)\n- (ordinary product ad)\n- (random clutter)\n- (copying real logos)\n= [THE OUTPUT]\n\n[INSTRUCTION]\nRender the visual solution to the equation above.\n\nThe subject must become a handcrafted miniature world that explains, celebrates, and physically builds itself.\n\nVISUAL LOGIC:\n- The subject’s identity becomes either a giant edible landscape, oversized word monument, open-book story scene, or object-shaped collection.\n- Its materials become tactile and transformed: cookie, cream, felt, clay, paper, fabric, wood, crumbs, seeds, tiny props, or miniature objects.\n- Its message becomes readable physical typography, banners, signs, plaques, labels, category names, or mottoes.\n- Its activity becomes tiny workers, fans, makers, explorers, builders, players, chefs, or visitors interacting with the subject.\n- Its softer emotional side becomes pastel textile relief, felt plants, stitched details, padded clouds, tiny homes, and gentle handmade scenery.\n- Its informational side becomes organized zones, callouts, labels, object clusters, icons, arrows, and category groupings.\n\nCOLOR / MATERIAL:\n- Base: cream, warm beige, ivory, soft paper white.\n- Accents: blue, red, coral, yellow, teal, mint, sage, chocolate brown, black, gold.\n- Materials: food textures, matte clay, soft felt, painted wood, fabric, paper, foam, tiny model props.\n\nOUTPUT:\nA viral miniature artifact where $ SUBJECT becomes part edible landscape, part tiny construction site, part open-book story, part soft textile world, and part physical infographic.",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four handcrafted miniature worlds, each built from a lesser-known Middle Eastern street food. Every panel turns its subject into a giant edible landscape where the food's own materials become terrain — layered pastry cliffs, a river of sesame paste, dunes of spiced rice, folded flatbread hills. Tiny workers, chefs and visitors climb, cook and explore across each landscape at model scale. The dish's name rises as physical typography built from the food itself, with small banners, signs, plaques and category labels placed through the scene like an infographic. Softer areas become pastel textile relief — felt plants, stitched details, padded clouds, tiny handmade houses. Base palette of cream, warm beige, ivory and soft paper white with accents of blue, red, coral, yellow, teal, mint, sage, chocolate brown and gold. Materials read as food texture, matte clay, soft felt, painted wood, fabric, paper and foam. No ordinary product-ad look, no random clutter, no real logos.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**프롬프트를 방정식으로 쓴다.** gdgtify 계열 문법 실험의 또 다른 갈래:\n\n```\n($ SUBJECT)\n+ (giant edible landscape)          ← 거대 식용 지형\n+ (tiny worker typography world)     ← 작은 일꾼 + 물리적 타이포\n+ (open-book clay story diorama)     ← 펼친 책 점토 디오라마\n+ (soft pastel textile relief)       ← 파스텔 직물 부조\n+ (object-shaped flat-lay infographic)\n- (ordinary product ad)              ← ★뺄셈으로 금지 지정\n- (random clutter)\n- (copying real logos)\n= [THE OUTPUT]\n\n[INSTRUCTION] Render the visual solution to the equation above.\n```\n\n★배울 점 — **`+`가 스타일 합성, `−`가 네거티브 프롬프트 역할**을 한다. 금지를 별도 섹션에 몰아 적는 대신 같은 식 안에 두니 \"무엇을 더하고 무엇을 빼서 이 결과가 나오는가\"가 한눈에 읽힌다.\n\n★그리고 아래에 **`VISUAL LOGIC` 6줄이 변환 규칙**을 준다 — 주제의 각 측면을 무엇으로 바꿀지:\n- 정체성 → 거대 식용 지형 / 대형 단어 기념비 / 펼친 책 장면 / 오브젝트 모양 컬렉션\n- 재료 → 촉각적 변환(쿠키·크림·펠트·점토·종이·직물·나무·부스러기·씨앗)\n- 메시지 → **읽히는 물리적 타이포**(배너·간판·명판·라벨·카테고리명)\n- 활동 → 작은 일꾼·팬·제작자·탐험가·요리사·방문객\n- 정서 → 파스텔 직물 부조·펠트 식물·박음질 디테일·패딩 구름\n- 정보 → 구획된 존·콜아웃·아이콘·화살표·분류 묶음\n→ 라이브러리의 [[gdgtify-product-material-to-world-physics]]와 같은 뿌리(제품→지형)지만, 여기서는 **감정·정보 측면까지 물리적 재료로 번역**한다.",
