      "category": "제품/광고",
      "title": "★★\"제품이 장면 안에 놓이는 게 아니라 장면을 서서히 잠식한다면?\" — 제품의 재질 하나가 환경 전체로 번지게",
      "prompt": "Use the uploaded product image as the single source of truth.\n\nSilently analyze the product’s category, function, audience, emotional promise, brand personality, materials, colors, textures, patterns, packaging, typography, logo behavior, and most ownable visual characteristic.\n\nCreate a premium campaign image where one distinctive material, texture, pattern, or physical behavior extracted from the product begins spreading through the surrounding environment—as though the product’s identity is taking possession of the scene.\n\nThe transformation must originate naturally from the real product and expand across nearby surfaces, architecture, atmosphere, or landscape.\n\nExamples:\n\n— airflow sculpting the room into smooth aerodynamic ribbons\n— outdoor fabric and mountain textures reclaiming an urban environment\n— triangular chocolate geometry spreading through refined architecture\n— controller symbols and illuminated circuitry reshaping a dark gaming space\n\nThe environment must remain readable while becoming unmistakably connected to the brand. Avoid random decoration. Every transformed element must communicate the product’s real function, personality, or emotional promise.\n\nPRODUCT DNA LOCK:\n\nPreserve the product exactly: shape, proportions, structure, packaging, logo, label, typography, colors, materials, textures, finishes, reflections, and all visible details.\n\nDo not redesign, recolor, relabel, distort, simplify, duplicate, or invent product features.\n\nSilently generate five different takeover concepts. Score each for visual hook, originality, brand fit, instant readability, realism, product focus, and commercial strength. Reject anything generic, decorative, or below 9/10. Produce only the strongest concept.\n\nCreate one unique two-word slogan based on the selected brand and transformation. Do not reuse “Texture Takeover.” Match the brand’s authentic language, typography, scale, placement, and visual tone.\n\nComposition: one hero product, one clearly traceable transformation origin, controlled visual spread, refined negative space, premium editorial framing, realistic material transitions, cinematic commercial lighting, precise contact shadows, tactile micro-details, and clean hierarchy.\n\n16:9. One standalone campaign image. No grid, no collage, no split screen, no miniature world, no infographic icons, no arrows, no floating labels, no repeated products, no unrelated props, no mockup presentation, no random text.\n\n────────── ※트윗 본문 ──────────\nGPT Image 2 Prompt: Texture Takeover\n\nWhat if the product didn’t sit inside the scene, but slowly possessed it?\n\nLet one signature material spread through the world until the entire frame feels unmistakably branded.\n\nFull prompt in the next comment ⬇️ https://t.co/Rjjw8rojI6",
      "gen_prompt": "A premium campaign image in which one signature material extracted from the product has begun spreading through the surrounding environment, as though the product's identity were taking possession of the scene. A dark bar of chocolate stands as the hero on a plinth, and the triangular prism geometry of its segments propagates outward — first into the plinth's edge, then into the steps, the wall panels and finally the coffered ceiling of a refined minimal interior, every surface resolving into the same repeating triangular ridge. The transformation is clearly traceable back to the bar itself, radiating from the point where it rests. The architecture stays completely readable as a room even as it becomes unmistakably branded. Warm cocoa browns and burnished gold against pale stone, cinematic commercial lighting, realistic material transitions, precise contact shadows, tactile micro-detail, refined negative space, wide 16:9. One standalone image — no grid, no collage, no split screen, no miniature world, no infographic icons, no floating labels, no random text.",
      "prompt_ko": "★질문 하나로 컨셉이 정의된다:\n> **\"제품이 장면 **안에 놓이는** 게 아니라, 장면을 **서서히 잠식한다면** 어떨까?\"**\n> *\"하나의 시그니처 재질이 세계로 퍼져나가, 프레임 전체가 명백히 그 브랜드로 느껴질 때까지.\"*\n\n★번짐의 규칙이 명확하다:\n```\n· 변형은 **실제 제품에서 자연스럽게 시작**되어(originate naturally from the real product)\n  주변 표면·건축·대기·풍경으로 확장된다\n· 환경은 **읽히는 상태를 유지**하면서 브랜드와 명백히 연결돼야 한다\n· ★**임의의 장식은 금지**(Avoid random decoration).\n  변형된 모든 요소는 제품의 **실제 기능·개성·정서적 약속**을 전달해야 한다\n```\n\n★예시가 그 원리를 보여준다 — 전부 **제품의 본질**에서 나온 재질이다:\n| 제품 | 번져나가는 것 |\n|---|---|\n| 공기청정/에어 제품 | 기류가 방을 매끄러운 **공기역학 리본**으로 조각 |\n| 아웃도어 의류 | **야외 원단과 산의 질감**이 도시 환경을 되찾음 |\n| 삼각 초콜릿 | **삼각 기하**가 정제된 건축을 관통해 번짐 |\n| 게이밍 기기 | 컨트롤러 심볼과 **발광 회로**가 어두운 공간을 재구성 |\n\n- 이 계정의 시그니처 3종 세트가 완성됐다 — [[aziz4ai-product-shaped-void-campaign]](제품을 **빼서** 판다) · [[aziz4ai-product-reflection-metaphor-campaign]](**반사**가 정체를 드러낸다) · 그리고 이번 **번짐**. 셋 다 `PRODUCT DNA LOCK` + `5안 생성·채점·9/10 미만 기각` 구조를 공유한다.\n- 슬로건 규칙도 동일: **두 단어**, 그리고 *\"'Texture Takeover'를 재사용하지 마라.\"*",
