      "prompt": "Modified the previous style a little bit. Still works great for albums (I am using Nano Banana).\n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 famous albums in <style =  $ SUBJECT\n\n// Analyze subject as an iconic myth, object, figure, place, creature, or concept.\nCORE = infer_iconic_identity($ SUBJECT)\nSYMBOLS = infer_symbolic_motifs($ SUBJECT)\nARCHITECTURE = infer_environmental_geometry($ SUBJECT)\nTITLE = generate_short_albumlike_title($ SUBJECT)\n\n// Build framed monochrome poster.\nFRAME = construct_deco_frame(\n  style = 'black-and-white Art Deco stained-glass poster',\n  border = 'thick black frame with inner silver/white linework',\n  geometry = ['arches', 'sunbursts', 'gear rings', 'triangular panels', 'stepped corners', 'ornamental plaques'],\n  texture = 'slight screenprint grain, crisp ink edges'\n)\n\n// Transform the subject.\nSUBJECT_PANEL = transform(\n  CORE,\n  into = 'central stained-glass / album-cover icon',\n  rules = [\n    'preserve the subject silhouette clearly',\n    'convert surfaces into black, white, and gray geometric panels',\n    'convert curves into elegant Deco arcs and leaded-glass outlines',\n    'convert small details into gears, rays, windows, medallions, stripes, or symbolic linework',\n    'make the subject feel monumental, mysterious, and poster-readable'\n  ]\n)\n\n// Fill world around subject.\nSYMBOLIC_WORLD = populate(\n  source = SYMBOLS + ARCHITECTURE,\n  elements = [\n    'tiny city silhouettes',\n    'machine-age structures',\n    'abstract landscapes',\n    'radiating suns',\n    'clockwork motifs',\n    'futuristic towers',\n    'ritual-like icons',\n    'small narrative silhouettes'\n  ],\n  placement = 'inside and around the central subject panel'\n)\n\n// Add typography as graphic ornament.\nTYPE = add_title_system(\n  title = TITLE,\n  style = 'condensed Art Deco uppercase lettering',\n  placement = ['top banner', 'bottom plaque', 'small side label'],\n  accuracy = 'decorative, inferred, not dependent on perfect text'\n)\n\nRENDER:\n- $ SUBJECT becomes a framed monochrome album-poster relic.\n- Use pure black, ivory white, silver gray, and no bright color.\n- The layout should feel like a collectible stained-glass concert poster or museum print.\n- Prioritize bold silhouette, ornamental symmetry, crisp line hierarchy, and graphic drama.\n- Avoid photorealism, color gradients, messy sketching, modern UI, and direct copies of existing album/movie titles.>",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid of four black-and-white Art Deco stained-glass posters, each transforming a different iconic subject into a monumental central icon. Every panel sits inside a thick black frame with inner silver linework, built from arches, sunbursts, gear rings, triangular panels, stepped corners and ornamental plaques, carrying a slight screenprint grain and crisp ink edges. In each, the subject's silhouette stays clearly readable while its surfaces convert into black, white and grey geometric panels, its curves become elegant Deco arcs and leaded-glass outlines, and its small details turn into gears, rays, windows, medallions and symbolic linework — monumental, mysterious and poster-readable. Around and inside the central panel, a symbolic world fills the space: tiny city silhouettes, machine-age structures, radiating suns, clockwork motifs, futuristic towers and small narrative figures. Condensed Art Deco uppercase lettering runs across a top banner and a bottom plaque with a small side label. Pure monochrome, no colour anywhere.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**의사코드 파이프라인**이다. 대문자 상수에 분석 결과를 담고, 함수로 변환해 흘려보낸다:\n```\n// 주제를 신화·사물·인물·장소·개념으로 분석\nCORE         = infer_iconic_identity($SUBJECT)\nSYMBOLS      = infer_symbolic_motifs($SUBJECT)\nARCHITECTURE = infer_environmental_geometry($SUBJECT)\nTITLE        = generate_short_albumlike_title($SUBJECT)\n\nFRAME = construct_deco_frame(style=..., border=..., geometry=[...], texture=...)\n\nSUBJECT_PANEL = transform(CORE, into='central stained-glass icon', rules=[\n    '실루엣을 명확히 보존하라',\n    '표면을 흑·백·회 기하 패널로 변환하라',\n    '곡선을 우아한 데코 아크와 납선 윤곽으로 변환하라',\n    '작은 디테일을 기어·광선·창·메달·줄무늬·상징 선묘로 변환하라'])\n\nSYMBOLIC_WORLD = populate(source=SYMBOLS+ARCHITECTURE, elements=[...],\n                          placement='inside and around the central subject panel')\nTYPE = add_title_system(title=TITLE, style='condensed Art Deco uppercase', ...)\n```\n\n★`transform()`의 **rules 배열이 진짜 설계**다. 스테인드글라스로 바꾼다는 건 결국 **표면 → 기하 패널 / 곡선 → 납선 아크 / 디테일 → 상징 선묘**라는 세 개의 치환이다. 그걸 규칙으로 나열하니 어떤 주제를 넣어도 같은 변환이 적용된다.\n\n- 첫 줄의 `preserve the subject silhouette clearly`가 가드레일이다. 양식화가 강한 스타일일수록 **원형이 사라지는 게** 실패다.\n- 앨범 커버가 소재인 것도 잘 맞는다 — 정사각 프레임 + 중앙 아이콘 + 상하 조판은 앨범 재킷의 문법 그대로다.\n\n---\n★**한 계정이 프로그래밍 패러다임을 바꿔가며 쓴 프롬프트 컬렉션**이다. 지금까지 확인된 것만 일곱 가지 —\n```\n함수형(p5.js)   [[gdgtify-p5js-artdeco-generative-grid]]\nJSON 구조체     [[gdgtify-single-panel-meme-cartoon-json]]\n가중치 수식     [[gdgtify-weighted-formula-negative-space-poster]]\n최적화 문제     [[gdgtify-optimization-objective-infographic]]\nSQL 질의       [[gdgtify-sql-select-city-portrait]]\nSQL 뷰/DDL     [[gdgtify-sql-view-handheld-planet]]\n상태 기계       [[gdgtify-state-machine-clay-timeline]]\n클래스 정의     [[gdgtify-python-class-contradiction-grid]]\n의사코드 파이프 [[gdgtify-pseudocode-deco-album-poster]]\n```\n공통점은 **자연어로 쓰면 뭉개지는 관계를 문법으로 고정**한다는 것이다. 무엇이 입력이고 무엇이 파생인지, 무엇이 우선이고 무엇이 금지인지가 코드 구조상 분명해진다.",
