      "prompt": "This prompt was made for Midjourney but I haven't used MJ for a while now. It works well with GPT though. Here is the prompt for books: \n\n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 non-copyrighted books: {$SUBJECT, flat cel-shaded illustration with heavy uniform dark ink contours, engraved technical-plate linework, panel seams and fine interior hatching, stepped flat fills with hard shadow terminators, desaturated bone and steel-grey base palette, sky graded from cool slate navy to warm amber, electric white and oxide red accents only, broad backlit ambient light, rim-lit silhouettes, no cast shadows, perfectly clean digital surface with zero grain or texture, detail concentrated on the primary mass and sparse elsewhere, near-orthographic perspective, low horizon, generous negative sky, monumental stillness}",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four monumental book-cover illustrations: top left Moby-Dick with a whale's back breaking a flat sea, top right Frankenstein with a lone tower on an ice field, bottom left The Time Machine with a vast seated sphinx on a plain, bottom right Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea with a submarine hull rising from still water. Flat cel-shaded illustration with heavy uniform dark ink contours, engraved technical-plate linework, panel seams and fine interior hatching, stepped flat fills with hard shadow terminators, desaturated bone and steel-grey base palette, sky graded from cool slate navy to warm amber, electric white and oxide red accents only, broad backlit ambient light, rim-lit silhouettes, no cast shadows, perfectly clean digital surface with zero grain or texture, detail concentrated on the primary mass and sparse elsewhere, near-orthographic perspective, low horizon, generous negative sky, monumental stillness.",
      "prompt_ko": "중괄호 하나에 스타일 전체를 담되, **구절마다 담당 영역이 다르다**. 형용사 나열처럼 보이지만 실제로는 표를 한 줄로 편 것이다:\n\n```\n{$SUBJECT,\n  선   → heavy uniform dark ink contours / engraved technical-plate linework / fine interior hatching\n  면   → stepped flat fills            (계단식 평면 채움)\n  그림자 → hard shadow terminators, no cast shadows   ★그림자 경계는 딱딱하게, 드리운 그림자는 금지\n  팔레트 → desaturated bone + steel-grey 기반\n         sky graded cool slate navy → warm amber       ★하늘만 그라데이션 허용\n         electric white + oxide red accents **only**   ★악센트를 2색으로 제한\n  광원  → broad backlit ambient, rim-lit silhouettes\n  표면  → zero grain or texture                        ★질감 완전 금지\n  밀도  → detail concentrated on the primary mass, sparse elsewhere  ★디테일 예산 배분\n  원근  → near-orthographic, low horizon, generous negative sky}\n```\n\n★**`detail concentrated on the primary mass and sparse elsewhere`** 한 줄이 이 스타일의 핵심이다. 어디에 디테일을 쓸지 예산을 배분해 두면 나머지가 저절로 비워진다 — 같은 원리의 심화판이 [[gdgtify-spatial-frequency-band-detail-budget]].\n\n★작성자 주: **미드저니용으로 만들었는데 GPT에서 더 잘 나온다**. 모델 간 프롬프트 이식성의 사례.\n\n---\n★재현 방식 교체 — 처음엔 한 장으로 그리드를 시켰는데 **Krea2가 칸마다 같은 구도를\n반복**해서 원본과 딴판이 나왔다. 주제를 gen_prompt에 정확히 적어놔도 그렇다 — 지시를 못 따르는 게\n아니라 **단일 이미지 확산 모델이라 칸마다 다른 의미를 배정하지 못하는 것**이다.\n→ **칸마다 한 장씩 뽑아 합성**하고, Krea2가 못 쓰는 영문 타이포는 코드로 얹었다.\n   정본 스크립트 `automation/grid_repro.py` + spec `automation/grid_specs/gdgtify-celshaded-engraved-book-grid.json`.\n   런북 §gen_prompt ④ 참조.",
