      "id": "gdgtify-python-class-noir-raincut-rewrite",
      "source": "https://x.com/Gdgtify/status/2081557182122955084",
      "author": "Gdgtify",
      "date": "2026-07-27",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "아트 포스터",
      "title": "★같은 그림을 다른 문법으로 다시 쓴 사례 — 느와르 레인컷을 파이썬 클래스 + 함수 호출로 재작성 (원판은 RENDER_CHAIN 문법)",
      "prompt": "4 detective books visualized with GPT Image 2. \n\nPrompt: \n2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 non copyrighted books real book about crime/police/detectives:: <instructions> class MonochromeNoirRaincut: \n    def __init__(self, subject=\"$SUBJECT\"):\n        self.subject = subject\n        self.illustration = self.__infer__()\n    def __infer__(self):\n        noir = NoirIllustration()\n        # convert identity to angular graphic distortion\n        noir.silhouette = convert_to_angular_planes(self.subject, style='sharp geometry, wedge-like')\n        noir.shading = apply_chiaroscuro(self.subject, blacks='deep', highlights='white cutout', grays='hatching')\n        noir.texture = apply_scratchboard_grain(self.subject, detail='rain streaks, crosshatch, stipple')\n        # environment\n        noir.background = towering_noir_cityscape(vertical_silhouettes=True, mist=True, perspective='low-angle')\n        noir.atmosphere = heavy_rain_lines(diagonal=True) + backlit_glow() + fog_bands()\n        # composition\n        noir.frame = 'dramatic low-angle, subject foreground silhouette against bright misty glow'\n        noir.finish = 'black-and-white, no color, high-contrast graphic poster, film noir frozen storm'\n        return noir\n    def render(self):\n        return render_noir_poster(self.illustration, avoid=['color', 'photorealism', 'soft airbrush', 'glossy 3D', 'cute', 'clean vector', 'bright even light'])\nexec(MonochromeNoirRaincut().render()) </instructions>",
      "gen_prompt": "A 2x2 grid, 16:9, of four black-and-white film-noir poster illustrations for classic detective novels — a trench-coated investigator, a fedora silhouette at a doorway, a lone figure under a streetlamp, and a figure descending a fire escape. Each subject is converted into angular graphic planes with sharp wedge-like geometry, shaded in hard chiaroscuro with deep blacks, white cut-out highlights and grey hatching, surfaced with scratchboard grain of rain streaks, crosshatch and stipple. Behind each figure a towering noir cityscape of vertical building silhouettes fades into mist, seen from a low angle. Heavy diagonal rain lines, backlit glow and bands of fog fill the air. Dramatic low-angle framing places the subject as a foreground silhouette against a bright misty glow. High-contrast graphic poster, film noir frozen storm, black and white only. No colour, no photorealism, no soft airbrush, no glossy 3D, no cute styling, no clean vector, no bright even light.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**같은 그림을 다른 문법으로 다시 쓴 실물 사례**다. 라이브러리에 이미 있는 [[gdgtify-monochrome-noir-raincut-poster-grid]]와 **결과물은 같은 계열인데 프롬프트 문법이 완전히 다르다** — 원판은 `RENDER_CHAIN`/`MORPH_RULES` 블록형이었고, 이번엔 파이썬 클래스다:\n\n```python\nclass MonochromeNoirRaincut:\n    def __infer__(self):\n        noir = NoirIllustration()\n        # 정체성을 각진 그래픽 왜곡으로 변환\n        noir.silhouette = convert_to_angular_planes(subject, style='sharp geometry, wedge-like')\n        noir.shading    = apply_chiaroscuro(subject, blacks='deep',\n                                            highlights='white cutout', grays='hatching')\n        noir.texture    = apply_scratchboard_grain(subject,\n                                            detail='rain streaks, crosshatch, stipple')\n        # 환경\n        noir.background = towering_noir_cityscape(vertical_silhouettes=True, mist=True,\n                                                  perspective='low-angle')\n        noir.atmosphere = heavy_rain_lines(diagonal=True) + backlit_glow() + fog_bands()\n        # 구도\n        noir.frame  = 'dramatic low-angle, subject foreground silhouette against bright misty glow'\n        noir.finish = 'black-and-white, no color, high-contrast graphic poster, film noir frozen storm'\n        return noir\n\n    def render(self):\n        return render_noir_poster(self.illustration,\n            avoid=['color','photorealism','soft airbrush','glossy 3D','cute','clean vector','bright even light'])\nexec(MonochromeNoirRaincut().render())\n```\n\n★이 판본의 이점은 **`+` 연산자**다. `heavy_rain_lines(diagonal=True) + backlit_glow() + fog_bands()` — 대기 효과 세 겹이 **더해진다는 것**이 문법으로 드러난다. 자연어로 쓰면 '비, 역광, 안개'가 되고 셋의 관계가 사라진다.\n\n★`avoid=[...]`를 **render()의 인자로** 넣은 것도 눈여겨볼 만하다. 네거티브가 별도 문단이 아니라 렌더 호출의 파라미터가 된다.\n\n★그리고 마지막 줄 `exec(...)` — 클래스를 정의하고 **실행까지 시킨다**. 정의만 하고 끝나는 프롬프트와 구분되는 마무리다.\n\n같은 계정 클래스 문법 계열: [[gdgtify-python-class-contradiction-grid]] · [[gdgtify-python-hybrid-style-engine-mix]] · [[gdgtify-taxonomic-silhouette-microobject-flatlay]]",
