      "prompt": "I have been doing these split screen prompts for a couple of years now. This one is Nano Banana Pro vs. GPT Image 2. Subjects are different because of GPT's restrictions. \n\n<instructions> SUBJECT            ::= [character / android / antihero / fashion warrior / mythic figure] DUALITY            ::= [memory vs erasure / human vs machine / pristine vs ruined / past vs present] COSTUME_LOGIC      ::= [elegant battlewear / ceremonial armor / noir couture / tactical dress] FRACTURE_TYPE      ::= [crack / rain seam / glass split / burn scar / glitch divide] SURFACE_CONTEXT    ::= [grunge wall / stained concrete / rain glass / ruined shrine / urban decay] MATERIAL_FALLOUT   ::= [water / ash / dust / paint peel / static / shattered lacquer] FORMAT             ::= 16:9 LAYOUT ::= +--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+ |                        atmospheric negative space / wall text                  | |                                                                                | |          [ SUBJECT dominant, offset slightly from center ]                     | |                                                                                | |               left side = intact identity                                      | |               center    = FRACTURE_TYPE vertical/semi-vertical axis            | |               right side = decay / reveal / alternate state                    | |                                                                                | |     edge details = rain, scratches, stains, symbolic marks, broken texture     | +--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+ INSTRUCTION ::= Generate SUBJECT as a widescreen fractured icon portrait. The image should not just split the face aesthetically; the FRACTURE_TYPE must function as a narrative axis dividing two states of identity. Make the materials around the split meaningful and tactile.",
      "gen_prompt": "A widescreen fractured icon portrait of an android in ceremonial battlewear, positioned dominant and offset slightly from centre. A vertical rain-seam splits the frame: the left side shows the intact identity, the right side shows decay and the machine state revealed beneath. The seam is not merely aesthetic — it functions as a narrative axis dividing two states of identity, human versus machine. Materials around the split are tactile and meaningful: water, ash, peeling paint, shattered lacquer. Background is a stained concrete wall with rain glass; edge details include scratches, stains and symbolic marks. Atmospheric negative space across the top. 16:9.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**레이아웃을 글자로 그려 넘기는 문법.**\n\n```\nLAYOUT ::=\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              분위기 있는 여백 / 벽면 텍스트                    |\n|        [ SUBJECT 우세, 중앙에서 살짝 비껴서 ]                  |\n|            왼쪽  = 온전한 정체성                              |\n|            중앙  = FRACTURE_TYPE 수직축                       |\n|            오른쪽 = 부패 / 드러남 / 다른 상태                  |\n|   가장자리 = 비, 긁힘, 얼룩, 상징 자국, 깨진 질감              |\n+--------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n★**INSTRUCTION 한 줄이 이 프롬프트를 완성한다**:\n*\"얼굴을 미학적으로 쪼개기만 하지 마라. **균열이 두 상태를 가르는 서사의 축으로 기능해야 한다.**\"*\n\n분할 초상은 흔하지만 대개 \"예쁘게 갈라진 얼굴\"에 그친다. 갈라짐에 **의미(기억↔소거,\n인간↔기계, 온전↔폐허)** 를 부여하라고 못박은 게 차이다.\n\n★변수를 맨 위에 `::=`로 선언(SUBJECT / DUALITY / COSTUME_LOGIC / FRACTURE_TYPE / …)해서\n같은 틀로 다른 주제를 돌릴 수 있게 만들었다.",
      "ref_image": null,
