      "id": "vigo-cobalt-megatype-roadside-travel",
      "source": "https://x.com/vigocreativeai/status/2082100038012911905",
      "author": "vigocreativeai",
      "date": "2026-07-29",
      "lang": "en",
      "target_model": "GPT Image 2",
      "category": "포스터/타이포",
      "title": "★목적지가 아니라 '지나치는 정류장'을 판다 — 훔칠 만한 트릭 셋을 본인이 적어둔 건",
      "prompt": "VISUAL OS 008 — Cobalt Roadside Travel\n\nTravel posters sell destinations. These four sell the parts you're supposed to sleep through:\n\n- NORTH TRAM — a valley station at first light — ascend\n- RIVER BATH — a neighborhood bathhouse at dusk — warmth\n- OPEN SIGNAL — a desert radio relay — listen\n- SEA GATE — a ferry pier, 06:30 local — depart\n\nA landmark asks to be admired. A tram stop asks to be remembered. The second one stays with you longer.\n\nThree tricks worth stealing:\n\n1. The headline doesn't fit the page — both words crop past the left edge. A word too big for the paper reads like a place too big for the trip.\n2. Two voices, one blue: machine-cut megatype up top, one hand-painted verb down on the asphalt. The type names the place; the handwriting tells you what to do there.\n3. The paper is cold, the photo is warm. Everything graphic prints in a single cobalt — so the whole poster reads as a two-color riso run, and the amber light has to come from the world, not the palette.\n\nLocked: cream uncoated paper, cropped cobalt megatype, straight-on golden-hour architecture shot, blue micro-poem, one painted verb across the dark foreground\n\nSwaps: place name / building type / locator + micro-poem / the verb\n\nThe destination is optional. The stop is the point.\n\nPrompt ↓\n\n[답글] Copy the whole block, swap only the 5 fields at the bottom:\n\n{\n  \"style\": \"cobalt-megatype-roadside-travel-editorial\",\n  \"aspect_ratio\": \"4:5\",\n  \"style_rules\": [\n    \"poster splits near the middle: cream editorial field above, full-width documentary location photograph below\",\n    \"two enormous stacked words in ultra-heavy italic condensed sans, one saturated cobalt #0754AD, cropping decisively past the left edge, slightly weathered ink edges\",\n    \"upper-right stays open with a tiny locator system: thin horizontal rule, small label stack, circular icon, outlined capsule\",\n    \"a short compact cobalt micro-poem sits low in the cream field\",\n    \"photograph is straight-on, eye-level and wide: one low building or transport structure spanning the frame, warm amber light against a petrol-charcoal foreground\",\n    \"one oversized loose hand-painted cobalt word across the dark road, water or ground at the bottom\",\n    \"palette locked to warm cream #EEE6D6, cobalt #0754AD, faded amber-orange, petrol green, lifted charcoal — no pure black\",\n    \"fine analog grain, offset-print speckle, mild halftone and subtle ink misregistration unify type and photo\"\n  ],\n  \"MAIN_TEXT\": \"NORTH TRAM\",\n  \"PAINTED_WORD\": \"ascend\",\n  \"LOCATION_SUBJECT\": \"a small wooden tram station in a cedar forest at first light, one vintage green tram waiting, wet rails and morning fog\",\n  \"LOCATOR_TEXT\": \"VALLEY LINE / PLATFORM TWO / MORNING CLIMB\",\n  \"MICROCOPY\": \"First light slips into the cedar valley. The car waits in silence. The climb takes time. No rush.\"\n}",
      "gen_prompt": "A two-colour riso-style travel poster, 4:5. The poster splits near the middle: a warm cream uncoated editorial field above, a full-width documentary location photograph below. Two enormous stacked words, NORTH TRAM, in ultra-heavy italic condensed sans, a single saturated cobalt, cropping decisively past the left edge with slightly weathered ink edges. The upper right stays open with a tiny locator system: a thin horizontal rule, a small label stack, a circular icon, an outlined capsule. A short compact cobalt micro-poem sits low in the cream field. The photograph is straight-on, eye-level and wide: a small wooden tram station in a cedar forest at first light, one vintage green tram waiting, wet rails and morning fog, warm amber light against a petrol-charcoal foreground. One oversized loose hand-painted cobalt word reading ascend runs across the dark ground at the bottom. Palette locked to warm cream, cobalt, faded amber-orange, petrol green and lifted charcoal — no pure black. Fine analog grain, offset-print speckle, mild halftone and subtle ink misregistration unify type and photo.",
      "prompt_ko": "★**이 배치에서 가장 값어치 높은 건.** 프롬프트가 JSON 슬롯이고, 게다가\n**\"훔칠 만한 트릭 3가지\"를 본인이 직접 적어뒀다.**\n\n먼저 기획 논지가 좋다:\n> *\"여행 포스터는 목적지를 판다. 이 넷은 당신이 자는 동안 지나치기로 되어 있는 부분을 판다.\"*\n> *\"랜드마크는 감탄해 달라고 한다. 전차 정류장은 기억해 달라고 한다. 뒤엣것이 더 오래 남는다.\"*\n> *\"목적지는 선택이다. 정류장이 요점이다.\"*\n\n★**훔칠 만한 트릭 셋** (원문 그대로):\n\n```\n1. 헤드라인이 지면에 안 들어간다 — 두 단어 모두 왼쪽 가장자리를 넘어 잘린다.\n   종이에 비해 너무 큰 단어는 여행에 비해 너무 큰 장소처럼 읽힌다.\n\n2. 두 개의 목소리, 하나의 파랑 — 위쪽은 기계로 재단한 메가타입, 아래 아스팔트에는\n   손으로 칠한 동사 하나. 활자는 장소의 이름을 대고, 손글씨는 거기서 무엇을 할지 말한다.\n\n3. 종이는 차갑고 사진은 따뜻하다 — 그래픽 요소는 전부 코발트 한 색으로만 인쇄해\n   포스터 전체가 2도 리소 인쇄로 읽히게 하고, 앰버 빛은 팔레트가 아니라\n   세계에서 와야 한다.\n```\n\n★**JSON 슬롯 구조**다 — `style_rules` 8줄은 잠그고 **아래 5칸만 바꿔** 시리즈를 찍는다.\n\n| 잠금(Locked) | 교체(Swaps) |\n|---|---|\n| 크림 비도공지 / 잘린 코발트 메가타입 / 정면 골든아워 건축 사진 / 파란 마이크로 시 / 어두운 전경을 가로지르는 손그림 동사 | `MAIN_TEXT` 장소명 · `LOCATION_SUBJECT` 건물 유형 · `LOCATOR_TEXT` 위치 + `MICROCOPY` 마이크로 시 · `PAINTED_WORD` 동사 |\n\n★색을 **헥사로 못박은 것**도 실무적이다 — `#EEE6D6`(웜 크림), `#0754AD`(코발트),\n그리고 **\"순수 검정 없음\"**. 2도 인쇄 느낌은 검정이 끼면 바로 깨진다.\n\n★네 장의 시리즈가 각각 **장소 + 시각 + 동사** 세 조각으로 이뤄진다 —\nNORTH TRAM(첫 빛의 계곡역 / ascend), RIVER BATH(황혼의 동네 목욕탕 / warmth),\nOPEN SIGNAL(사막 무선 중계소 / listen), SEA GATE(06:30 페리 부두 / depart).",
